From 3750b3491f1f4e579e0e1588a89bb051e62fd62a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:56:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Propose M4 particle sampling: decisions, contract,
 independent tests

M4 design-and-test proposal on the verified M3 baseline (a6726c4); no
production M4 code.

- DM4-1..DM4-17: minimal scope (uniform-parameter and equal-distance
  sampling, reusable arc-length table, explicit seam policy, explicit
  limits); randomness, area distributions and emission deferred.
- Contract: six public types in workshop.vfx.math.sample; normative,
  deterministic algorithm (globally adaptive 5-point Gauss-Legendre with
  bisection error estimate, safeguarded Newton-bisection inversion);
  work bounds in curve evaluations; failure policies.
- 44 independent tests (exact, closed-form and 1e-28 quadrature oracles,
  metamorphic, adversarial, determinism, boundary) and 3,064 reference
  rows from a stdlib-only generator; regeneration byte-identical.
- Evidence: 298/298 against a throwaway reference; all 336 reference
  lengths converge with error <= 0.31 tau; 28 of 33 mutants killed,
  the rest equivalent or tolerance-equivalent.

M1, M2 and M3 are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
